  "news_brief": "* **AMD \u2014 Sector & Guidance Contagion:** \"AMD's stock slides after Intel earnings reveal two big issues\" (Morningstar / Dow Jones, 2026-10-30) \u2014 Shares plunged nearly 11% ahead of AMD's Nov. 3 earnings report after rival Intel issued a weak Q4 forecast, citing an industrywide 20% decline in PC shipments, inflated memory-chip prices, and server CPU supply constraints.\n* **AVGO \u2014 Sector Selloff, Insider Activity & Financing Risk:** \"Why is Broadcom stock sliding today?\" (Investing.com, 2026-10-30) \u2014 Broadcom dropped ~5.5% amid the Intel-driven semiconductor rout and anxiety over hyperscaler AI capex, compounded by a William Blair downgrade, an Oct. 29 Form 4 insider trading filing, and concerns over $43 billion in potential backstop exposure tied to an Anthropic asset-financing deal.\n* **NVDA \u2014 Antitrust Regulation & Export Rule Scrutiny:** \"Nvidia Stock (NVDA) Falls 0.8% to $213.66 (Oct 29)\" (Gotrade, 2026-10-30) \u2014 Shares slipped alongside broader tech weakness as investors digested reports of a U.S. Department of Justice antitrust inquiry into Nvidia's planned $12.9 billion acquisition of Hugging Face, as well as comments from CEO Jensen Huang regarding a Singapore customer under U.S. investigation for potential export control bypasses.\n* **NVDA \u2014 Sector Selloff & Customer Credit Guarantees:** \"NVIDIA (NASDAQ:NVDA) Stock Price Down 4.2% - Here's Why\" (MarketBeat, 2026-10-30) \u2014 Following Thursday's dip, Nvidia fell another 4.2% on Friday to $204.64 amid sector-wide AI capex and memory-cost fears after Intel and Amazon results, alongside reports that Nvidia may guarantee credit for a customer's data center buildout.\n* **MSFT \u2014 Company Earnings & Cloud Guidance:** \"Microsoft Rises on Double Beat as Azure Growth Accelerates\" (TheStreet Pro, 2026-10-28) \u2014 Microsoft initially climbed in after-hours trading after reporting a fiscal Q1 2027 beat ($92.28 billion revenue, $4.92 GAAP EPS) driven by 48% Azure growth and strong Q2 constant-currency Azure growth guidance of 49%\u201350%, though shares pared gains on Oct. 29 amid broader AI sector selloffs.\n* **MSFT \u2014 Capital Expenditure Debt Financing & Downgrade:** \"Microsoft Stocks Decline With $1.28 Billion in Annual Fixed Coupons\" (GuruFocus / TradingView, 2026-10-30) \u2014 Shares fell 1.6% to close the week around $521.91 following an analyst downgrade and a $25 billion debt offering priced on Oct. 29 to fund heavy data center capital expenditures ($45.2 billion in Q1), which depressed quarterly free cash flow year-over-year.",
